# dotenv environment variable files
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
# Committed on purpose: holds only the public Worker URL for native builds.
!.env.capacitor

# Cloudflare / Wrangler
.wrangler
.dev.vars
.dev.vars.*
# Committed template so a fresh clone knows which secrets to fill in.
!.dev.vars.example

# The native projects are committed on purpose. `cap add ios|android` generates
# them, but they are not disposable: the Android manifest carries the
# RECORD_AUDIO declaration the voice session needs, and regenerating the
# platform would silently drop it. Capacitor ships a .gitignore inside each
# platform that already excludes build output, `local.properties` and the
# copied web assets, so tracking the folder costs almost nothing.
